272		// Make the data durable before claiming it: a plain registration at
273		// seq 0 persists the table only, while an advance must barrier the
274		// target and every earlier committed batch even when Options.Sync is
275		// false. The current segment goes through its live write handle;
276		// rolled segments are closed and reopened just for the fsync. A
277		// failure leaves the in-memory checkpoint untouched and the whole
278		// call retryable.
279		if seq > 0 {
